      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\n  if (encr_enable) {\n    if (!BTM_ReadRemoteVersion(p_dev_rec-\u003eble.pseudo_addr, \u0026remote_lmp_version,\n                               nullptr, nullptr)) {\n      LOG_WARN(\"BLE Unable to determine remote version\");\n    } else if (remote_lmp_version \u003e\u003d HCI_PROTO_VERSION_5_2) {\n      /* Link is encrypted, start EATT if remote LMP version 5.2 or greater */\n      bluetooth::eatt::EattExtension::GetInstance()-\u003eConnect(\n          p_dev_rec-\u003eble.pseudo_addr);\n    }\n  }\n```\nI suppose that we don\u0027t want to encrypt if the `BTM_ReadRemoteVersion` has failed.\nWhat do you think of using else if instead ?\n\nI also removed the `if (remote_lmp_version` part of it as it already checked by the `\u003e\u003d` next to it\n\nI also removed the log of `remote_lmp_version` since it\u0027s value is `0` on `BTM_ReadRemoteVersion` failure.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1592,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1603,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "aa2a86619188acc4b66d5e3b210a700b12f902b8",
